    "checks": [
      "Only an existing carriage house or garage may become an ADU. It may be enlarged, but then the district dimensional rules apply (1.04.005(c)(4))",
      "The principal house must be an owner-occupied single-family dwelling. The ADU must be removed or converted back when that ends (1.04.005(c)(1) and (2))",
      "The ADU must be licensed under the city rental housing rules and tenants registered (1.04.005(c)(9)). Article 1761 lists an ADU as a tenant-occupied unit",
      "RS2, UN1, UN2, MUI1 and MUI2 tables set a 20 ft minimum building height for 'All' uses. Whether it reaches an enlarged garage is not stated",
      "Article 1761 counts 'a short-term lodging accommodation' and 'an accessory dwelling unit' as tenant-occupied units that need a rental license (1761.03(k)). No zoning ban on short-term rental was found",
      "An accessory building may not exceed 50% of the first floor building area of the principal structure (1304.02 7.01(b)(2))",
      "1303.06(g)(2) lets a rear building be used as an ADU only if it 'conforms with all use, height and area requirements' and the house is owner-occupied. It is a limit, not a second grant. The ADU still needs the 1.04.005 special exception and an existing carriage house or garage",
      "Undersized lot: the ADU text does not require a conforming lot. District dimensions apply only if the garage is enlarged ('setbacks, building area', 1.04.005(c)(4)). 1306.01(b)(2) allows 'the establishment of a use on any nonconforming lot'. 1303.06(g)(2) requires a rear dwelling building to meet 'area requirements', which may include lot area. Ask the Zoning Officer"
    ],
    "notes": "Zoning office: Bureau of Planning and Zoning, https://www.yorkcity.org/decd/bureau-of-planning-and-zoning/. Pending changes: no ADU ordinance found. A news aggregator mentioned a Planning Commission text amendment on the RS1 single-family definition. Not confirmed and not law."
